WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:08.000
A cryptographically secure, on-chain list of two hundred and eighty million verified supporters is not an "analogy" or a

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.760
"metaphor" or a "nice idea.". It is the largest political mandate in human history.

3
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.600
Nothing else comes close. Politicians can ignore protests. They can ignore polls.

4
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:26.020
They can ignore reality for surprisingly long periods (see: climate change, nineteen seventy to present).

5
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:34.880
They cannot ignore two hundred and eighty million cryptographically verified humans saying "do this thing or we vote you

6
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.020
out.". Here's how to build that list. What You're Actually Building.

7
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.760
The Goal. Build a privacy-preserving, globally verifiable referendum.

8
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.820
It shows public support for a one percent treaty and decentralized institutes of health (D.I.H.).

9
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:58.660
Essentially, a website where people say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" in a way that lawyers find convincing.

10
00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:05.860
Requirements: Must be auditable (so politicians can't claim it's fake, though they will absolutely try).

11
00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.980
Must be persuasive (so policymakers actually do their jobs for once).

12
00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.020
Must hit three point five percent global participation (two hundred and eighty million plus verified votes).

13
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:26.440
That last number isn't arbitrary. Once three point five percent of a population actively supports something, it becomes

14
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:33.220
unstoppable. Every time. Across all cultures. For centuries.

15
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:42.700
More on that later. The Principles (Or: How Not to Build a Fraudulent Voting System): Verifiability: Cryptographic proofs

16
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.840
that votes are real (can't fake the math, though politicians will try).

17
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:55.740
Privacy: Nobody knows who you voted for (including us). Equity: Works for everyone, including people without bank accounts

18
00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:03.420
or government IDs (which is most of Earth, by the way). Transparency: Open-source code so anyone can audit it.

19
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:13.620
Viral Growth: Needs to spread organically. Target: ninety-nine percent detection, one point zero (each person brings more

20
00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:20.940
than one person, which is how avalanches work). Greater than ninety-nine percent fraud detection with less than one percent

21
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:29.500
false positives (the bots stay out, the humans stay in). Secondary metrics track geographic distribution, brand awareness,

22
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:35.900
and whether politicians have started sweating yet. (The sweat metric is informal but surprisingly reliable.

23
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:44.620
They always sweat before they act.). The Bottom Line. two hundred and fifty million dollars for the campaign, funded by

24
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:50.980
VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds. Target cost: less than one dollar per verified participant.

25
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.900
That's cheaper than acquiring a customer for literally any consumer product on Earth.

26
00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:06.020
You spend more marketing soda. two hundred and eighty million verified humans saying "do this or lose your job" to every

27
00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.320
politician on Earth. That's not a petition. Petitions are what you ignore.

28
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.590
That's a pink slip with two hundred and eighty million signatures.

29
00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:22.740
On Why three point five percent Is The Magic Number. The two hundred and eighty million target isn't pulled from thin air.

30
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:30.520
It's based on the "three point five percent Rule," a historical pattern that has held across cultures, centuries, and continents

31
00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:38.860
with the reliability of a physical law: When three point five percent of a population actively participates in sustained,

32
00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:47.800
nonviolent action, the movement wins. Every time. The evidence: Civil Rights (U.S.) crossed the three point five percent

33
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:55.120
threshold and ended segregation. Indian Independence crossed the three point five percent threshold and kicked out the British

34
00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.740
Empire. Women's Suffrage crossed the three point five percent threshold and won the vote.

35
00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:09.100
Once you hit three point five percent, three things happen simultaneously: it's clearly not a fringe movement, the support

36
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.580
is geographically distributed, and opposition becomes career suicide.

37
00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.959
Previous movements required marching in the rain, getting tear-gassed, or going to prison.

38
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.580
This one requires clicking a button from the toilet. The barrier to entry is lower.

39
00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:32.900
The incentive (healthcare you actually want) is higher. It's the easiest revolution in human history, which is fitting,

40
00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:39.260
because the problem (letting people die of curable diseases) is the stupidest crisis in human history.

41
00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.760
People show up for the healthcare. Politicians see two hundred and eighty million verified supporters.

42
00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:54.560
The treaty becomes inevitable. It's not manipulation. It's just understanding what motivates humans (not dying) and what

43
00:04:54.560 --> 00:05:00.820
motivates politicians (not losing elections). These two facts have been true for your entire history.

44
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.102
Nobody thought to combine them until now. *Source: Consolidated from global-referendum sub-files including implementation

45
00:05:04.102 --> 00:05:04.102
details, verification framework, and viral marketing strategies.*
